  "title": "# Build: follow-amber (Urgent profile) Brett, Nov 3 2026 (voice).",
  "asked": "# Build: follow-amber (Urgent profile) Brett, Nov 3 2026 (voice). Assigned agent: **Reel Rhonda** (book on her card; AXF_AGENT=reel-rhonda if supported). Register in Urgent (id `follow-amber`) + banner entry. ## What Brett wants One switch in the Dev Console: **'Follow Amber'** (Settings > Console, and a toggle in the context menu EVERYWHERE in the console via runtime context items, plus a small banner chip showing it's on). When it's ON: 1. **Amber opens windows as she talks about them.** Whenever Amber (Claude via axHub/axf-console MCP) mentions a console screen, dialog, build, PR, UI Review item, setting, plugin or anything that needs Brett, the console opens it on his screen right away (window/tab/dialog, focused, highlighted with the Go-to-it highlight). 2. **Approvals pop up in the console.** Every axHub held/confirm call for Brett (veto countdowns and straight approvals, including pass_grant) shows as a pop-up approval dialog in the console instead of making him go to axhub.amberxai.com: title + plain description, the exact call collapsible, countdown for veto items, big green Approve / red Deny (tap-to-confirm rules on touch per toolbar rule do NOT apply to these two; they act on one tap), queue if several. Decisions go to axHub signed as Brett (owner) - reuse axHub's approval API and the console's signed-in session; never lets an agent approve. 3. When OFF: nothing auto-opens, approvals only show in the normal approvals dialog/badge. ## How - Server: the console subscribes to axHub's approval/job event stream (SSE/websocket) for Brett; on a new held/confirm item -> push the dialog to every connected console client of his. Reuse console-wake (PR #266): if no console is open and the switch is on, wake it through AmberX so the dialog/window still appears. - MCP: add `console_follow` / make console_open / console_dialog / console_action ALLOW policy (no veto) when they only navigate/show (opening a screen, dialog, highlighting) - navigation never changes data, so it must never wait 90 s. Add a `console_show` tool: {target, highlight?, say?} that Amber calls whenever she mentions something; it's a no-op when the switch is off. Expose `console.follow` state so Amber knows if it's on. - Rule: add to shared RULES.md + CLAUDE.md: 'When Follow Amber is on, every time you mention something in the console, call console_show for it; approvals go to the console pop-up.' Commands declared once -> REST + MCP + CLI. - Coordinate with the toolbars build (toolbar-tap-confirm) and ui-review-shots only through framework APIs; don't edit their files. - Tests (event -> dialog, approve/deny round trip with a fake axHub, switch off = nothing opens, navigation tools have allow policy), phone + desktop screenshots, UI Review item, report `_claude/builds/reports/follow-amber.md`, THREADS, PR, steps through the store. Commits clean and professional. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once. Model switches (Brett, Nov 3 2026): a downgrade (e.g. Fable → Opus) is fine. An UPGRADE (e.g. Opus → Fable) needs Brett's approval: when you reach one, run `node apps/console-web/plugins/build-orchestrator/orchestrator.mjs request-upgrade <id> <phase>`, ask once, and stop. Never approve a model switch upgrade yourself (no `act approve` on an upgrade), never relaunch on a higher model.",
